{
 "name": "winged serpent (Ashcoil sky-wyrm)",
 "comment": "Bone head/tail in the rigger frame: Blender Z-up after its 180-degree Z turn, +Y forward (snout), left = -X. reference_bounds is the Ashcoil mesh bbox measured in that frame, so the fit is identity for this mesh. No legs at all: the whole trunk behind the wings is the tail_NN chain (14 segments, straight along -Y at z 0.046 -- the snake lies on the ground and rears its neck up to the head). Two wings mounted just behind the skull on the chest, four finger ribs each, tips measured at (0.58,-0.235,0.33) (0.494,-0.241,0.161) (0.374,-0.204,0.013) (0.255,-0.115,0.10) from the wrist knob at (0.205,0.02,0.29).",
