 "jaw_mask_comment": "The Embercrest gap-following mask does not fit this head, and the sculpt seals the mouth, so heat alone left the mandible 0.62 jaw / 0.37 head and the gape was a muzzle bend. This plane follows the lip crease measured in the side view (z 0.185 at y 0.27 falling to 0.171 at y 0.31, the mandible is the 0.02 below it) within the muzzle box |x|<0.035, y>0.25, blending in from the hinge over y 0.25..0.28 so the throat barbels stay heat-weighted.",
 "wing_bind_level_deg": 35,
 "wing_bind_level_comment": "The sculpt raises the arm 54 degrees from the shoulder; the Embercrest correction (35 at the root, -35 at the wrist) brings the outer membrane close to level for flight.",
 "wing_field": {
  "comment": "Membrane weight field gates, canonical space (= mesh space here). span_x starts past the 0.05 trunk half-width where the arm leaves the flank; span_z is negative so it never gates -- nothing but wing lives at |x|>0.07 on a legless body; fade_y is between the wrist knob (y 0.02) and the mane spikes (y>0.10, |x|<0.12) so the crest is never touched; hub is the wrist knob.",
